{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A density-functional study of CO adsorption on Pt(111): site preference, dispersion and the “CO/Pt puzzle”",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "F. Kohn, G. Sham",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We revisit the long-standing discrepancy between DFT and experiment for CO on Pt(111), where generalised-gradient functionals wrongly favour the fcc hollow over the observed atop site. Using plane-wave calculations with PBE, RPBE, BEEF-vdW and the hybrid HSE06 we show that the site ordering is controlled by the position of the CO 2π* level, and that HSE06 restores the experimental preference by 0.09 eV.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "DFT · adsorption · Pt(111) · CO · hybrid functionals",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Keywords"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Kohn–Sham density-functional theory ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "kohn1965"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the workhorse of surface chemistry, yet the simple case of CO on Pt(111) remains a known failure ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "feibelman2001"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Computational details",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Kohn–Sham equations",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\left[-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m}\\nabla^2 + v_{\\text{ext}}(\\mathbf r) + v_{\\text H}[n](\\mathbf r) + v_{\\text{xc}}[n](\\mathbf r)\\right]\\psi_i(\\mathbf r) = \\varepsilon_i\\,\\psi_i(\\mathbf r)",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:ks",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "were solved self-consistently with the density ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n(\\mathbf r) = \\sum_i^{\\text{occ}} |\\psi_i(\\mathbf r)|^2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Adsorption energies are defined as",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E_{\\text{ads}} = E_{\\text{CO/Pt}} - E_{\\text{Pt}} - E_{\\text{CO(g)}},",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:eads",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "so that negative values denote exothermic binding.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Code: plane-wave PAW, cutoff 450 eV",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Slab: 4-layer p(2×2) Pt(111), bottom two layers fixed, 15 Å vacuum, dipole correction",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "k-points: 8×8×1 Monkhorst–Pack, Methfessel–Paxton smearing 0.1 eV",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Forces converged to 0.02 eV/Å",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
