      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Within the Blyholder picture the bond is described by 5σ donation and 2π* back-donation. A Newns–Anderson estimate of the chemisorption energy is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\Delta E_{d} \\approx -2(1-f)\\frac{V^2}{|\\varepsilon_{2\\pi^*}-\\varepsilon_d|} - 2(f)\\frac{V'^2}{|\\varepsilon_d - \\varepsilon_{5\\sigma}|} + \\alpha V^2,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:newns",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "where ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\varepsilon_d",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the d-band centre. GGAs place 2π* too low, over-stabilising multi-fold sites where back-donation is stronger.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Vibrational analysis",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The C–O stretch frequency from the harmonic approximation is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\tilde\\nu = \\frac{1}{2\\pi c}\\sqrt{k/\\mu}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". HSE06 gives 2081 cm⁻¹ for atop CO, compared with the IRAS value of 2090 cm⁻¹.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Conclusions",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The CO/Pt puzzle is a self-interaction artefact: hybrid functionals correct the 2π* position and restore the atop preference.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
